%S A401241 0,1,1,1,1,2,1,2,1,2,1,2,1,2,2,2,1,2,1,2,2,2,1,3,1,2,2,2,1,3,1,2,2,2,
%T A401241 2,2,1,2,2,3,1,3,1,2,2,2,1,3,1,2,2,2,1,3,2,3,2,2,1,3,1,2,2,2,2,3,1,2,
%U A401241 2,3,1,3,1,2,2,2,2,3,1,3,2,2,1,3,2,2,2,3
%N A401241 The number of divisors of n that are prime powers (A246655) whose number of divisors is a power of 2.
%C A401241 First differs from A375272 and A385378 at n = 64.
%C A401241 Inverse Moebius transform of the characteristic function of the prime powers of the form p^(2^k-1), where p is prime and k >= 1. These prime powers are also the numbers m for which A064380(m) = A000010(m), i.e., the primes and the terms in A176509.
%H A401241 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A401241/b401241.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A401241 a(n) = Sum_{d|n} A069513(d)*A359473(d) =  Sum_{d|n} [A001221(d) = 1] * A209229(A000005(d)), where [] is the Iverson bracket.
%F A401241 Additive with a(p^e) = A000523(e+1).
%F A401241 Sum_{k=1..n} a(k) ~ n * (log(log(n)) + B + C), where B is Mertens's constant (A077761), C = Sum_{k>=2} P(2^k-1) = 0.183077059924063305405... (the sum of the reciprocals of the terms in A176509), and P(s) is the prime zeta function.
%t A401241 f[p_, e_] := BitLength[e + 1] - 1; a[1] = 0; a[n_] := Plus @@ f @@@ FactorInteger[n]; Array[a, 88]
%o A401241 (PARI) a(n) = vecsum(apply(x -> exponent(x+1), factor(n)[, 2]));
%Y A401241 Cf. A000005, A000010, A000523, A001221, A036537, A064380, A069513, A077761, A176509, A209229, A246655, A359473, A372380, A372502, A375272, A385378.
%K A401241 nonn,easy,new
%O A401241 1,6
%A A401241 _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 18 2026
